{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And kissed him.</b> It is pointed (with extraordinary dots). Know that every word that is dotted in all of Scripture serves to arouse attention to a matter, and here it teaches you that this kiss was not with his whole heart but a kiss of anger, in the manner of what is written (Proverbs 27:6): ״ונעתרות נשיקות שונא״. And the prophet, peace be upon him, came and explained (Amos 1:11): ״ויטרוף לעד אפו ועברתו שמרה נצח״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:19.595572565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}